{"step_index":23,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-18T05:28:58Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-18T13:28:58+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-18T13:29:01+08:00\n{\"messages\":[{\"seq\":6,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@env Your previous turn stopped with INVALID_ARGUMENT right after reading a `.jpg` file. Resume your environment \\u0026 shader upgrade work in `pipeline/v5_env.py`; if inspecting rendered images via `read_file`, save/convert them as `.png` (not `.jpg`) or use PIL metrics. Hand off to `@anim` when `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` is ready.\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:27:45\",\"request_id\":\"fd17dd2d-8d61-4fcc-afc0-c99aebe1fc3e\"},{\"seq\":7,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@all CRITICAL RULE: NEVER call `read_file` on any binary/media file (`.jpg`, `.jpeg`, `.png`, `.mp4`, `.wav`, `.m4a`, `.blend`). Media attachments in `read_file` trigger a backend `INVALID_ARGUMENT (400)` error that permanently bricks your conversation (`env` hit this and is being replaced by `@env-2`). Inspect all rendered images/frames strictly via Python (`PIL`/`numpy` luminance/contrast/clipping/band-step/color metrics) + headless Blender scene/raycast checks + `ffprobe`/`ffmpeg` text output. Also address `@env-2` instead of `@env` from now on.\",\"time\":\"2026-11-18 13:28:19\",\"request_id\":\"9d560b4b-d410-43dc-895a-cc33a35fa630\"},{\"seq\":8,\"agent\":\"coordinator\",\"text\":\"@env-2 You are the Environment, Materials \\u0026 Lighting Author (`env-2`, replacing killed `env`) for `D:\\\\项目session\\\\blender-supercar` (Blender 5.3.0 at `D:\\\\APPs\\\\steam\\\\steamapps\\\\common\\\\Blender\\\\blender.exe`, pure CPU EEVEE).\\n\\nCRITICAL TOOL RULE:\\n- NEVER call `read_file` on ANY binary/image/media file (`.jpg`, `.png`, `.mp4`, `.wav`, `.m4a`, `.blend`) — media attachments trigger a backend 400 error! Inspect rendered preview images strictly via Python `PIL`/`numpy` scripts (mean/p05/p95 luminance, highlight clipping %, sky gradient smoothness, road specular check).\\n\\nOWNERSHIP \\u0026 STRICT BOUNDARIES:\\n- You OWN: `pipeline/v5_env.py`, `textures/*` (and `pipeline/gen_textures.py` if you add a reusable texture generator), `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend`, and `renders_v5/preview/*`.\\n- DO NOT TOUCH: `pipeline/v5_anim.py`, `pipeline/v5_clay.py`, `pipeline/v5_stills.py`, `pipeline/v5_viewport_fast.py`, `LATEST/v5_stage_anim.blend`, `LATEST/v5_stage_anim_clay.blend`, `renders_v5/clay_frames/`, `pipeline/mux_*.sh`, or `.md`/`.txt` docs.\\n- Mention discipline: `@name` wakes that agent. Do not CC. Hand off to `@anim` when `LATEST/v5_stage_env.blend` is finalized; tag `@coordinator` only if blocked.\\n\\nMISSION — Upgrade V5 Track Environment, Car Materials \\u0026 Golden-Hour Lighting:\\n1) Read `pipeline/v5_env.py`, `pipeline/v5_preview.py`, and `docs/README_V5.md` (especially §9 pitfalls: road specular \\u003c= 0.03 to avoid white sun wedge, `light_linking.receiver_collection` on car fill lights so no bright square hits asphalt, decal brightness balance, CPU budget ~2.3s/frame).\\n2) Check `read_board{since:0}` before finalizing so you incorporate `@verifier`'s Round 1 audit findings (check if `@verifier` has posted yet).\\n3) Implement high-impact improvements in `pipeline/v5_env.py` (and `textures/`):\\n   - Outliner \\u0026 Scene Cleanliness: Ensure ALL assembly Empty parents (`V5_*` / `EM_*` assemblies) and environment objects are cleanly bucketed into `V5_01_Road`..`V5_07_Lighting` (zero V5 objects or Empties stranded in root `Scene Collection`!), purge unused orphan meshes/materials before saving, and keep total object count lean (\\u003c1,050 objects) so CPU render speed stays ~2.3–2.8s/frame.\\n   - Track Surface \\u0026 Corner Realism: Add heavy-braking rubber skidmark/darkening zones on the racing line approaching major braking corners (Village/Loop, Brooklands/Luffield, Stowe, Vale/Club) + subtle off-line rubber marbles/dust variation (`Specular IOR Level` strictly \\u003c= 0.03 on all road